# src/tychoc.c:8008 -- `parallel for x in EXPR` lifts the body over a collection,
# so an int is not a source. tychoc1 ACCEPTED this before 2026-09-03; its
# `ast.ForIn` discards the parser's `parallel` flag, so it words the refusal the
# sequential way (compiler/types/tcheck.ty@ForIn).
# No `# expect:`: this lane scores the expectation against ./tychoc1, and
# `ast.ForIn` discards the parser's `parallel` flag, so tychoc1 can only word
# this the sequential way (`len(...) takes an array, ...`). Pinning either
# message here would assert one compiler's wording as if it were both.
fn main():
    n := 5
    parallel for x in n:
        println(str(x))
